## Web Application Specification: Intelligent Invoice Batch Processor

### Core Concept
Build a browser-based SaaS application that enables accounting teams, freelancers, and small business owners to efficiently digitize paper and PDF invoices through an intuitive dual-mode extraction interface. The app combines manual region-based OCR with intelligent document attribute highlighting to create a hybrid human-in-the-loop data extraction pipeline.

### User Personas
- **Primary**: Bookkeepers processing 50-200 invoices weekly
- **Secondary**: Small business owners doing their own accounting
- **Tertiary**: AP (Accounts Payable) clerks in mid-size companies

### Feature Requirements

#### 1. Document Ingestion Pipeline
- **Batch PDF Upload**: Drag-and-drop or file picker accepting up to 50 PDFs simultaneously (max 25MB per file, 100MB total batch)
- **Multi-format Support**: PDF (primary), image files (JPEG, PNG, TIFF) as secondary inputs
- **Page Preview Generation**: Thumbnail generation for each page (150x200px) with lazy loading
- **Document Classification**: Auto-detect invoice vs. receipt vs. other document types
- **Duplicate Detection**: Hash-based duplicate detection with visual warning

#### 2. Dual-Mode Extraction Interface

**Mode A: Region-Based OCR (Canvas Interaction)**
- **Interactive Document Viewer**: PDF.js-based renderer with zoom (50%-400%), pan, and rotate capabilities
- **Bounding Box Drawing**: Click-and-drag to create resizable rectangular regions over text areas
- **Multi-Region Selection**: Allow multiple non-contiguous boxes per document
- **Region Types**: Assign semantic meaning to each box (Vendor Name, Invoice Number, Date, Line Items, Total Amount, Tax, etc.)
- **OCR Engine Integration**: Tesseract.js for client-side processing or cloud OCR API (Google Vision/AWS Textract) for server-side
- **Confidence Scoring**: Display OCR confidence per region (color-coded: green >90%, yellow 70-90%, red <70%)
- **Text Correction Panel**: Side-by-side view of extracted text with inline editing

**Mode B: Document Attribute Highlighting (Text Layer Interaction)**
- **Text Layer Rendering**: Extract and render selectable text overlay on PDF canvas
- **Semantic Highlighting**: Users highlight text spans to tag with predefined attributes:
  - Vendor Information (Name, Address, Tax ID)
  - Invoice Metadata (Number, Date, Due Date, PO Number)
  - Financial Data (Subtotal, Tax, Total, Currency)
  - Line Items (Description, Quantity, Unit Price, Amount)
- **Smart Snapping**: Auto-expand selection to word/line boundaries on double-click
- **Keyboard Shortcuts**: Quick-tagging via number keys (1=Invoice#, 2=Date, etc.)
- **Template Learning**: Suggest attribute locations based on previously processed invoices from same vendor

#### 3. Batch Processing Workflow
- **Queue Management**: Visual pipeline showing documents in stages (Uploaded → Processing → Review → Exported)
- **Bulk Actions**: Apply OCR regions or attribute mappings across similar documents in batch
- **Template System**: Save extraction patterns as templates for recurring vendors
- **Progress Persistence**: Auto-save progress every 30 seconds; resume interrupted sessions

#### 4. Data Validation & Output
- **Field Validation**: Regex patterns for common formats (dates, currency amounts, email addresses)
- **Cross-Field Logic**: Validate that Line Item sum equals Subtotal, Subtotal + Tax equals Total
- **Export Formats**: 
  - Structured JSON (per document and aggregated)
  - CSV/Excel spreadsheet
  - QuickBooks/Xero integration (OAuth API)
  - XML for ERP systems
- **Audit Trail**: Timestamped log of all extractions and corrections made

### Technical Architecture

**Frontend Stack:**
- React 18+ with TypeScript
- PDF.js for rendering and text extraction
- Fabric.js or Konva.js for canvas-based region drawing
- React-PDF or similar for thumbnail generation
- State management: Zustand or Redux Toolkit

**Backend Stack:**
- Node.js/Express or Python/FastAPI
- PostgreSQL for document metadata and extraction results
- Redis for job queues and caching
- S3/MinIO for document storage
- WebSocket server for real-time progress updates

**OCR Integration:**
- Primary: Google Cloud Vision API or AWS Textract (for accuracy)
- Fallback: Tesseract.js (for offline capability and cost reduction)
- Custom model endpoint for specialized invoice formats (optional)

**Infrastructure:**
- Docker containerization
- Horizontal scaling for batch processing workers
- CDN for static assets and thumbnails

### UI/UX Design Specifications

**Main Interface Layout:**
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  HEADER: Logo | Batch Progress | User Menu | Export      │
├──────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│          │                                              │
│  THUMB-  │         DOCUMENT VIEWER                      │
│  NAIL    │         (PDF Canvas + Text Layer)            │
│  PANEL   │                                              │
│          │         [Toolbar: Zoom | Pan | Draw | Text]  │
│          │                                              │
│          ├──────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│          │         EXTRACTION PANEL                     │
│          │         [Tabs: Regions | Attributes | Data]  │
│          │                                              │
└──────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

**Interaction Flow:**
1. User uploads batch → sees thumbnail grid
2. Clicks first document → opens in viewer
3. Selects extraction mode (Region OCR or Attribute Highlight)
4. Performs extraction → sees extracted data in side panel
5. Reviews/edits extracted fields
6. Marks document as complete → moves to next in batch
7. Bulk exports when batch complete

**Key Interactions:**
- **Region Drawing**: Click start → drag → release → select field type from dropdown → OCR runs automatically
- **Text Highlighting**: Triple-click to select line → assign attribute from floating toolbar → value appears in data panel
- **Template Application**: "Apply to Similar Documents" button suggests matches based on vendor name detection

### Data Model (Core Entities)

**Document**
- id, filename, file_path, page_count, upload_timestamp, status, user_id

**ExtractionRegion**
- id, document_id, page_number, x, y, width, height, field_type, raw_text, confidence_score, corrected_text

**DocumentAttribute**
- id, document_id, field_name, value, confidence, source (auto|manual), position_data

**ExtractionTemplate**
- id, user_id, template_name, vendor_pattern, region_mappings, attribute_rules

### Security & Compliance
- End-to-end encryption for documents at rest (AES-256)
- TLS 1.3 for data in transit
- SOC 2 Type II compliance roadmap
- GDPR-compliant data retention (auto-delete after configurable period)
- Role-based access control (Admin, Booker, Viewer)

### Pricing Model (Optional)
- Freemium: 50 pages/month free
- Pro: $29/month for 1000 pages
- Business: $99/month for 5000 pages + API access
- Enterprise: Custom volume pricing

### Success Metrics
- Average time to process 50 invoices: <15 minutes (target: <5 minutes with templates)
- OCR accuracy: >95% for printed text, >85% for handwritten
- User retention: 70% return within 7 days

